Skip a file whose size exactly equals the remaining hexdump/od skip.
When the skip covered a whole regular file, the file was passed over by
reducing the skip without seeking, then reading went on to the next
file. A skip exactly equal to the file's size also took this path, but
left a skip of zero, which next() treats as positioned and ready, so
the file was dumped from its start instead of being skipped. Only take
the shortcut when the skip exceeds the size; an equal skip now seeks to
the end of the file as any smaller skip seeks within it.

---
 libbb/dump.c |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/libbb/dump.c
+++ b/libbb/dump.c
@@ -347,9 +347,9 @@
 	xfstat(STDIN_FILENO, &sbuf, fname);
 #endif
 	if (S_ISREG(sbuf.st_mode)
-	 && dumper->pub.dump_skip >= sbuf.st_size
+	 && dumper->pub.dump_skip > sbuf.st_size
 	) {
-		/* If st_size is valid and pub.dump_skip >= st_size */
+		/* If st_size is valid and pub.dump_skip > st_size */
 		dumper->pub.dump_skip -= sbuf.st_size;
 		dumper->pub.address += sbuf.st_size;
 		return;
